{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 25, :comments ["<b>Therefore.</b> Because they abandoned His Torah." "<b>And the mountains quaked.</b> From the weight of the blow." "<b>Tossed.</b> Cast down, and the kaf is a root letter, and like it שרופה באש כסוחה (burned with fire, tossed) (Psalms 118[?]), and the two share the same pattern."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 5, :notes {2 "The citation תהלים פ' י\"ן (Psalms 80:17) does not contain this phrase; the verse with כסוחה is Psalms 118:27, so the citation as given in the Hebrew may be corrupt."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:51:56.153367263Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}